venv/
frontend/
node_modules/
# Raw/processed/synthetic data and any locally-built Chroma index are
# dev-only and excluded - but the image builds its own fresh index at
# docs/knowledge_base/ build time (see the Dockerfile's
# build_knowledge_base.py step) and writes it to this same data/chroma_db/
# path via a RUN step inside the container, not via COPY from the host,
# so this exclusion never applies to it. The negation below exists only
# so that stays true even if a future `COPY data/ data/` is ever added.
data/
!data/chroma_db
mlruns/
mlruns.db
notebooks/
tests/
.git/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
*.log
# docs/ is deliberately NOT excluded - the Dockerfile's
# build_knowledge_base.py build step needs docs/glossary.md,
# docs/decisions.md, and docs/knowledge_base/*.md to build the RAG index.
